cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formal research artifact, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Lean LFM-to-Dirac Derivation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Partin"
    given-names: "G. D."
version: "0.30.0-research-dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gpartin/LeanDiracDerivation"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A noncanonical Lean 4 research derivation through DIRAC-030. It connects a
  positive two-field C19 action to a massive C19 Klein-Gordon tangent and
  proves that a cubical four-component Dirac Hamiltonian squares to its
  continuum symbol. It controls lattice/time corrections and derives the
  positive-frequency density/current limit from the same action. It also
  formalizes copy exchange under cube translation and a conditional cubical
  spin-one-half representation with exact conventional-spin intertwiners,
  explicit spectrum, continuous unitarity, 2pi sign reversal, 4pi return,
  and quarter-turn plus all-angle interpreted-Hamiltonian covariance. Within
  a stated real local flavor-preserving cubical-incidence class it also
  classifies the continuum square root independently on both rank-four
  copies and proves the C19 scalar-symbol zero census. It also proves a finite
  positive-frequency spectral transport theorem and an explicit coherent
  finite spatial Fourier transport theorem with a proved periodic cubic
  character-to-momentum bridge, Parseval density, integrated current, and a
  finite-update pointwise phase-error bound. It further derives the native
  zero-momentum rest frequency, opposite-energy rest phases, and the doubled
  relative phase of a coherent branch pair without adding a clock rule.
  It further derives the free-continuum zitterbewegung velocity and position
  expectations from the existing Hamiltonian momentum response, including
  the exact native frequency and amplitude with explicit coherence controls.
  It then derives the phase accumulated along the native current trajectory,
  energy-clock reciprocity, the relativistic moving-clock factor, and
  directional group/phase-velocity reciprocity from that same continuum
  dispersion and current map, without assuming a Lorentz-factor rule.
  It further proves that one independently derived zitter observable period
  returns density, velocity, and position while negating the coherent
  four-component state; two periods return the state. Those endpoint actions
  equal the separately derived cubical 2pi and 4pi spinor actions on both
  retained copies, while the temporal and spatial generators are proved
  distinct.
  It further derives the longitudinal velocity operator from the existing
  Hamiltonian momentum response and proves that its normalized rms fluctuation
  in every nonzero positive-frequency mode equals the independently derived
  moving/rest phase-clock ratio, with an exact velocity-clock Pythagorean
  identity.
  It additionally derives free Lorentz boosts, the Pauli--Lubanski
  spin-one-half invariant, the Wigner--Thomas half factor, free charge
  conjugation, and the Gordon current decomposition from the same established
  four-component sector without changing the native action.
  Arbitrary nonlocal
  or flavor-mixing roots, exact native finite-spacing packet evolution,
  uniform fixed-physical-time convergence, nonlinear realization on a
  localized carrier, localized native zitterbewegung, an SI
  electron mass, a physical electron, and electromagnetic coupling remain
  open. This
  development version is newer than the archived v0.15.0 release.
